course: dictionary
lesson: 15922
title: Unprecedented
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The start of this word, un-, often means "not". A precedent is something that happened earlier and can be used as an example. So unprecedented means there was no earlier example: it has never happened before.
explain: «The town had unprecedented rainfall this summer, more rain than anyone had ever recorded.» The clue is "more than anyone had ever recorded". Nobody had seen rain like that before, so unprecedented means never seen before, or bigger than ever before.
explain: «The museum welcomed an unprecedented number of visitors on its first weekend.» The clue is the number: people came in a bigger crowd than the museum had ever known. Always check your meaning by swapping in "never happened before" or "more than ever before" and seeing if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Unprecedented is an adjective, so it describes a noun, such as a storm, a number or a rise.
fact: «Unprecedented» means never happened or done before; the first of its kind.
fact: «Unprecedented» can also mean much greater than ever before, as in «unprecedented numbers».
fact: It is a formal word, common in the news and in exam writing.
fact: In maths and science, an unprecedented value is higher or lower than every earlier record.
exercise: «The team's win was unprecedented: no club had ever done it before.» What does unprecedented mean? | *Never done before | Done every day | Very small | Boring
exercise: Ben says unprecedented means ordinary. Is he right? | Yes, it means common in the news | *No, it means never happened or done before | No, it means happening often | Yes, it means ordinary
exercise: «The heatwave brought unprecedented temperatures, hotter than any summer on record.» What does the sentence tell us? | The temperatures were cold | The temperatures were normal | The temperatures fell slowly | *The temperatures were higher than ever before
test: «The scientist recorded an unprecedented drop in the river level.» What does unprecedented tell us about the drop? | *The drop was lower than every earlier record | The drop happens every spring | The drop was very small and boring | The drop was the usual size
test: Sara says unprecedented means common. Which is correct? | It means common | It means ordinary and everyday | *It means never happened or done before | It means happens every week
exam: «The island had an unprecedented storm, the first in recorded history.» What does unprecedented mean here? | Very quiet | Happening every year | Easy to forecast | *Never happened before
